COMM ---------------------------------------------------------------------
COMM 15O(alpha,gamma)19Ne radiative capture: 15O beam on an at-rest alpha
COMM (He gas target). This is dragon_2014_DSSSD.dat/dragon_2003.ffcards's
COMM own reaction -- see README.md's "Reaction specification" for the
COMM full derivation and cross-checks against those files' own numbers.
COMM Loaded by ReactionConfig::Load() (see include/ReactionConfig.hh for
COMM the card format); consumed by ReactionKinematics (generic, not
COMM specific to this reaction) via PrimaryGeneratorAction's reaction-file
COMM constructor. Format modeled on this project's own dragon_2003.ffcards.
COMM ---------------------------------------------------------------------
COMM
COMM Ground-state masses, AME mass-excess convention (mass = A*amu +
COMM massExcessMeV, amu=931.49432 MeV/c^2) -- src/ureact.f case(2)'s own
COMM devmass values for BEAM/RECL; TARG's massExcessMeV (2.42492 MeV, the
COMM real AME value for 4He) reproduces src/ureact.f's own literal
COMM hemass constant (4.002603250*amu) to 7 eV, so this file uses the
COMM same mass-excess convention for every particle rather than mixing
COMM conventions.
COMM
BEAM 8   15   2.8554
TARG 2   4    2.42492
RECL 10  19   1.7511   4
COMM
COMM Resonance energy: CM energy above the 15O+alpha threshold at which
COMM the compound state (Ex=4.03 MeV in 19Ne, the astrophysical
COMM breakout resonance) forms. src/ureact.f case(2)'s own hardcoded
COMM value -- cross-validated in README.md against every independent
COMM number this repo's data files give for this configuration.
COMM
ERES 0.5036
COMM
COMM Bound excited states of 19Ne below the resonance that this cascade
COMM can pass through on its way to the ground state. Level numbers are
COMM this file's own labels (arbitrary positive integers, need not be in
COMM energy order) -- src/ureact.f's own idpart numbers for the same
COMM three states were 82, 83, 84; renumbered here to 1, 2, 3 rather than
COMM carried over literally (idpart is a GEANT3 tracking-medium/particle-
COMM table implementation detail, not a property of the physics).
COMM
COMM level  excitation(MeV)  lifetime(s)
LEVL   1     1.536             2.8E-11
LEVL   2     0.275             6.3E-11
LEVL   3     0.238             2.6E-8
COMM
COMM Branching ratios (src/ureact.f case(2)'s own gsdk brat/mode arrays):
COMM the resonance (-1) decays 80% direct to ground (this is the
COMM dominant branch this pilot's own two-body-only generator used to be
COMM limited to before cascade support existed), 15% to level 2 (0.275
COMM MeV), 5% to level 1 (1.536 MeV); level 1 then decays 95% to level 3
COMM (0.238 MeV) and 5% to level 2; levels 2 and 3 both decay 100% direct
COMM to ground. Percentages are renormalized per fromLevel by
COMM ReactionKinematics, so they don't strictly need to sum to 100 (they
COMM do here, matching the source exactly).
COMM
COMM fromLevel  percent  toLevel
BRAT   -1         80.0     0
BRAT   -1         15.0     2
BRAT   -1          5.0     1
BRAT    1         95.0     3
BRAT    1          5.0     2
BRAT    2        100.0     0
BRAT    3        100.0     0
COMM
SENT
